Data sources read at runtime
----------------------------

ClearShelf reads these sources only through Zetaris. No bulk data from them
is distributed in this repository.

Open Food Facts
  Data from Open Food Facts (openfoodfacts.org), ODbL.
  Database: Open Database License 1.0,
  https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
  Contents: Database Contents License 1.0,
  https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1-0/
  The intake manifest (data/manifest/skus.json) holds, for 40 products,
  the barcode, product name and brand, language, allergen, trace and
  label tags and a hash of the ingredient text, fetched from Open Food
  Facts on 23 Oct 2026 (SGT). It holds no ingredient text.

openFDA food enforcement reports (U.S. Food and Drug Administration)
  Public domain / CC0 1.0. ClearShelf is not endorsed by the FDA.
  The intake manifest quotes recall numbers, dates, classifications,
  statuses, firm names and recall reasons from these reports.

UK Food Standards Agency food alerts
  Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government
  Licence v3.0.
  https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/


Regulatory reference
--------------------

data/reference/market_allergens.json is transcribed, with a citation on
every row, from:
  - the Food Standards Agency allergen guidance for food businesses
    (GOV.UK) and Regulation (EU) No 1169/2011 Annex II on
    legislation.gov.uk: contains public sector information licensed under
    the Open Government Licence v3.0;
  - U.S. Food and Drug Administration guidance on food allergen labelling
    (FALCPA, the FASTER Act, Questions and Answers Edition 5): a work of
    the U.S. government.


